WEBVTT

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:11.280
It's finally time!

00:00:11.710 --> 00:00:15.000
Yes. Let's put our faith in Kasumi-san.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.780
On Stage A, we have the third game 
of the second round match.

00:00:18.780 --> 00:00:22.200
It's the second half of the fifth 
players' match, East Hand 1, bonus 2.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.040
And play begins!

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.510
Bonus 2

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:32.510
Second Half - East Hand 1

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:44.310
<i>I'm on top now, but my lead's 
so small that I can't relax yet.</i>

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>I'm still going!</i>

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:47.560
Pon!

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:50.590
Anetai declares another pon.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.030
<i>Oh, my.</i>

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:58.340
<i>If I stay on the defensive, we 
won't even make it to second place.</i>

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:21.050
<b>The Nationals</b>

00:02:32.770 --> 00:02:37.780
<b>Hand 11: 
Threat</b>

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:42.510
Wow, this place is so big!

00:02:42.510 --> 00:02:45.270
This is the entrance to the shrine.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:49.520
It's a bit of a walk yet before 
we get to the main shrine.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:49.000
Iwato Kasumi

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:49.000
9 Years Ago
Age 8

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:50.600
Okay!

00:02:54.340 --> 00:03:00.870
Grandmother, what is the princess like?

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:03.280
She looks very much like you.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:05.090
In the branch families,

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:09.040
you are the most closely related to the princess.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:13.540
That is why you will become a living talisman doll.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:20.770
The princess is host not only 
to the nine goddesses,

00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:24.580
but on very rare occasions, 
horrifying things also descend to her.

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:29.790
You will become the vessel for those 
things in her stead, and tame them.

00:03:32.530 --> 00:03:36.070
<i>Yes, Grandmother.</i>

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:39.590
<i>I will use them now.</i>

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:10.850
Kasumi-chan...

00:04:13.850 --> 00:04:15.100
This is bad.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:56.370
Tsumo.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:00.940
That'll be 3,200, 6,200.

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:03.240
It's a haneman!

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:07.890
Breaking Miyamori's streak here in 
the second half is Eisui's Iwato!

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:08.910
Excellent.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.170
<i>She won.</i>

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:17.670
<i>I might have to put them all into 
effect in order to deal with her.</i>

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.340
<i>The girl from Kagoshima....</i>

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:23.170
<i>seems like a different person all of a sudden.</i>

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:28.940
That's the...

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:33.320
Yes. She used it.

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:34.840
She hasn't done that in a while.

00:05:37.520 --> 00:05:38.950
Princess!

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:41.690
Is it all right for you to be awake?

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:44.050
I'm fine.

00:05:44.050 --> 00:05:47.070
How's the game going?

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:51.190
Kasumi-chan just won with a haneman. 
She's in second place.

00:05:52.310 --> 00:05:54.100
<i>Kasumi-chan...</i>

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:56.700
Miyamori's Bonus Hand 2 as 
dealer is over and we now

00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:59.580
move on to East Hand 2 
with Himematsu as dealer.

00:06:00.330 --> 00:06:02.740
<i>What's up with this table?</i>

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:05.670
<i>I wasn't expecting a monster show like this.</i>

00:06:06.290 --> 00:06:09.090
<i>I just want to play some normal mahjong.</i>

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:13.090
<i>It's not fun to come into 
the fifth players' match with</i>

00:06:13.090 --> 00:06:15.100
<i>everyone having the same number of points.</i>

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:18.730
<i>I want to give up. I want to quit.</i>

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:21.000
<i>This is too hard.</i>

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:25.360
<i>No. I can't give up now.</i>

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:27.510
<i>When you're up against monsters,</i>

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:30.110
<i>all an ordinary person can do is think.</i>

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:33.370
<i>If I were to stop thinking, 
ordinary is all I'll be!</i>

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:36.910
<i>I'll give the dice a spin, along with my brain!</i>

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:38.870
<i>I'm the dealer!</i>

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:40.290
East Hand 2

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:40.290
Dealer
Suehara Kyouko

00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:47.050
<i>All right.</i>

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:50.290
<i>What kind of trap are you going to set,</i>

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:54.040
<i>you boob-monster of Eisei?</i>

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:08.820
<i>I saw some footage of her playing 
at the regional tournament,</i>

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:11.200
<i>but I never saw her going on the offensive.</i>

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:14.230
<i>I can't make any reckless moves.</i>

00:07:32.260 --> 00:07:33.840
<i>Wait, this hand...</i>

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:35.880
<i>completely lacks any bamboos?!</i>

00:07:36.600 --> 00:07:38.840
<i>It's not like I was trying to do this.</i>

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:41.910
<i>I just haven't gotten a single 
bamboo in nine turns.</i>

00:07:44.770 --> 00:07:48.280
<i>It wouldn't be too unusual if it were just me,</i>

00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:51.370
<i>but looking at Miyamori's and Kiyosumi's discards,</i>

00:07:52.680 --> 00:07:55.590
<i>it'd seem like they have all-bamboo hands.</i>

00:07:56.360 --> 00:07:58.530
<i>But then there's Eisui...</i>

00:07:59.090 --> 00:08:03.080
<i>She's the only one discarding 
bamboos. Four, at that!</i>

00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:07.540
<i>So if Eisui's collecting bamboo,</i>

00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:11.300
<i>she could win at any time!</i>

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:14.800
Tsumo!

00:08:16.850 --> 00:08:18.060
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:22.640
Closed chinitsu, tsumo, iipeikou.

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:25.060
4,000. 8,000.

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:27.060
<i>She had nothing but bamboo?!</i>

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:30.230
<i>I'm done as dealer and I have to 
pay the baiman dealer penalty!</i>

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:33.800
<i>So if Miyamori and Kiyosumi didn't have</i>

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:35.700
<i>any bamboo in their hands, either...</i>

00:08:38.140 --> 00:08:40.630
<i>She built that hand without having to discard</i>

00:08:40.630 --> 00:08:42.460
<i>a single tile from another suit.</i>

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:47.890
<i>I don't know how to counter this!</i>

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:55.180
<i>Fallen to last...</i>

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:04.030
Suehara-senpai...

00:09:04.600 --> 00:09:08.110
She did it! We're in the lead!

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:11.360
She had a tough fight up to now.

00:09:11.360 --> 00:09:13.900
But it's from here on that's the problem.

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:16.240
You're right.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:18.260
<i>Well...</i>

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:22.700
<i>It's good that I made it to 
first place, but now what?</i>

00:09:23.270 --> 00:09:26.570
<i>Usually all I have to do is fortify my defenses,</i>

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.800
<i>but right now,</i>

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:35.050
<i>I can't switch back until Haru-chan 
or Tomoe-chan cleanse me.</i>

00:09:35.720 --> 00:09:37.830
<i>And since it's the second half,</i>

00:09:37.830 --> 00:09:41.010
<i>I can't get cleansed during the break.</i>

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:45.520
<i>Should I just stay in attack mode until the end?</i>

00:09:48.850 --> 00:09:51.290
East Hand 3

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:30.890
<i>What the hell is this?</i>

00:10:30.890 --> 00:10:32.670
<i>It's the character tiles now?</i>

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:35.980
<i>Miyamori and Kiyosumi...</i>

00:10:39.780 --> 00:10:41.560
<i>Have they noticed...</i>

00:10:41.560 --> 00:10:43.030
<i>this abnormal situation?</i>

00:10:45.810 --> 00:10:47.540
<i>She's the...</i>

00:10:48.130 --> 00:10:50.740
<i>She's the most dangerous player at Eisui!</i>

00:10:57.300 --> 00:10:59.320
It's the second half of the fifth players' match.

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:01.240
We're in the middle of East Hand 3.

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:05.130
Eisui's Iwato has a hand full of character tiles.

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:08.760
Actually, she won with a honitsu in East Hand 1,

00:11:08.760 --> 00:11:11.850
and then with a chinitsu just now.

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:13.780
It doesn't say in her data

00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:16.960
that she prefers single suit hands...

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:18.470
That's right.

00:11:18.470 --> 00:11:23.570
In her past games, she 
always had a defensive style.

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:26.550
I don't believe the data will 
show anything more than that.

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:27.970
Indeed.

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:33.640
So then, this may be her style 
when she goes on the offensive.

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:39.260
<i>I've got nothing but bamboo and circles.</i>

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:41.770
<i>But that reminds me.</i>

00:11:41.770 --> 00:11:44.040
<i>Back then, we played it all the time...</i>

00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:47.880
<i>Three player mahjong.</i>

00:11:54.770 --> 00:11:55.640
Chi!

00:11:58.360 --> 00:12:01.360
<i>You can't declare a chi in 
three player mahjong, though.</i>

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:04.690
<i>I'm glad Eisui's not sitting to my left.</i>

00:12:04.690 --> 00:12:07.370
<i>This means my hand will be 
faster than in three player.</i>

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:10.110
<i>Actually, this is totally different 
from three player mahjong.</i>

00:12:10.110 --> 00:12:11.980
<i>I understand that.</i>

00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:15.910
<i>And it doesn't change the fact 
that I'm at a disadvantage.</i>

00:12:16.670 --> 00:12:17.630
<i>But...</i>

00:12:24.630 --> 00:12:25.510
Pon!

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:28.970
<i>I'm used to three player mahjong.</i>

00:12:28.970 --> 00:12:31.500
<i>That's bound to give me a slight edge...</i>

00:12:35.010 --> 00:12:36.150
<i>making it easier</i>

00:12:38.260 --> 00:12:39.820
<i>to play here!</i>

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:41.570
Tsumo!

00:12:42.510 --> 00:12:43.800
1,000. 2,000.

00:12:47.670 --> 00:12:48.860
<i>I can do this.</i>

00:12:49.670 --> 00:12:53.160
Himematsu's Suehara wins this hand.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:54.370
Senpai!

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:56.170
Keep it up, Kyouko!

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:58.670
<b>Eisui Girls'</b>

00:12:56.900 --> 00:13:01.050
Someone else won. What's going on?

00:13:01.050 --> 00:13:02.760
She might have something

00:13:02.760 --> 00:13:05.750
that allows her to deal 
with Kasumi-san's power.

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:08.680
Earlier, I got the feeling 
that Kiyosumi let her call

00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:10.930
the eight of bamboo on purpose.

00:13:13.960 --> 00:13:15.440
It couldn't be...

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:18.020
Second Half - East Hand 4

00:13:15.690 --> 00:13:18.020
Dealer - Iwato Kasumi

00:13:22.450 --> 00:13:25.260
<i>This situation still isn't ending...</i>

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:29.740
<i>Looks like I'll have to make my move, then.</i>

00:13:30.610 --> 00:13:33.550
<i>I guess one win isn't enough to end this.</i>

00:13:34.070 --> 00:13:36.330
<i>Is this going to go on forever?</i>

00:13:36.830 --> 00:13:39.390
Kiyosumi's Miyanaga has yet to

00:13:39.390 --> 00:13:42.390
make a move in the second half of this match.

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:02.340
Nodoka, is something wrong?

00:14:02.800 --> 00:14:04.390
Saki-san just...

00:14:04.390 --> 00:14:06.570
Did something happen to Saki-chan?

00:14:06.890 --> 00:14:11.500
I feel like her expression changed just now.

00:14:11.500 --> 00:14:12.830
Her expression?

00:14:20.620 --> 00:14:21.460
Kan.

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:31.300
Riichi.

00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:32.790
<i>Riichi?!</i>

00:14:32.790 --> 00:14:34.810
<i>What the hell are you doing, Kiyosumi?</i>

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:38.310
<i>Not a rinshan kaihou, but a riichi?</i>

00:14:38.310 --> 00:14:42.690
<i>I guess she needed speed
 in order to edge in first.</i>

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:46.300
<i>But thanks to her, I should 
be in tenpai soon, too.</i>

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:48.320
<i>Senpu.</i>

00:14:46.800 --> 00:14:48.320
[Senpu, from the calendar of lucky and 
unlucky days, written as "first loses"]

00:14:49.650 --> 00:14:51.990
<i>If you rush in first, you lose!</i>

00:14:51.990 --> 00:14:53.990
If this passes, riichi!

00:14:56.230 --> 00:15:00.000
<i>I've got a 5-sided wait: 2, 5, 8 
of characters and 1, 4 of bamboo!</i>

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:02.120
<i>Miyamori's chasing her.</i>

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:06.000
<i>Now Kiyosumi will probably 
play into Miyamori's hand.</i>

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:10.830
<i>Didn't she see me test that in the first half?</i>

00:15:20.180 --> 00:15:22.580
<i>Eisui drew some honor tiles, as well.</i>

00:15:22.580 --> 00:15:25.380
<i>Yet, if the other three players</i>

00:15:25.380 --> 00:15:28.650
<i>continue this pattern of eliminating a suit...</i>

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:30.680
<i>Thinking about the number of tiles,</i>

00:15:30.680 --> 00:15:33.440
<i>there should be a surplus of 
circle tiles in the dead wall.</i>

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:38.290
<i>But the dora indicator isn't a circle tile.</i>

00:15:38.290 --> 00:15:41.380
<i>So does that mean Eisui's control</i>

00:15:41.380 --> 00:15:45.630
<i>doesn't extend to the deeper parts 
of the wall or the dead wall?</i>

00:15:46.360 --> 00:15:47.170
<i>The dead wall?</i>

00:15:47.530 --> 00:15:49.420
<i>You draw from it with a kan...</i>

00:15:50.570 --> 00:15:51.960
<i>So the dead wall draw!</i>

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:56.240
She got it!

00:15:56.240 --> 00:15:57.950
That's Toyone's winning tile!

00:15:57.950 --> 00:16:00.970
Yeah, but that's also kan material.

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:05.940
Another kan.

00:16:13.700 --> 00:16:17.240
Her earlier dead wall draw wasn't a circle tile.

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:22.460
That is to say, this is Iwato
Kasumi's current weak point!

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:30.710
She didn't negate Toyone's Senpu, either.
She actually accepted it in full.

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:34.220
This is the girl who defeated Amae Koromo:

00:16:34.220 --> 00:16:36.440
Kiyosumi's fifth player,

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:39.220
Miyanaga Saki!

00:16:41.420 --> 00:16:42.280
Tsumo.

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:43.640
Rinshan kaihou.

00:16:43.640 --> 00:16:45.500
2,000. 4,000.

00:16:49.760 --> 00:16:50.920
Okay!

00:16:51.430 --> 00:16:55.910
Kiyosumi High School's Miyanaga 
wins with a rinshan kaihou!

00:16:57.260 --> 00:17:01.060
All three of her wins in the 
first and second half have been

00:17:01.060 --> 00:17:05.920
through rinshan kaihou,
correct? This is amazing.

00:17:05.920 --> 00:17:08.430
Saki-chan won!

00:17:09.030 --> 00:17:10.920
Saki-san!

00:17:12.070 --> 00:17:15.200
With this, Kiyosumi leaps 
all the way to second place.

00:17:15.200 --> 00:17:16.890
Eisui stays in the lead,

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:20.890
and Himematsu once again falls to last place.

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:23.480
<i>I wanna give up...</i>

00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:26.190
But she just won...

00:17:26.190 --> 00:17:28.440
It's just beginning, Kyouko.

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:33.940
Second Half -  South Hand 1

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:33.940
Dealer - Anetai Toyone

00:17:29.600 --> 00:17:30.800
The game is now moving

00:17:30.800 --> 00:17:33.940
into the final South hand of 
the second round match.

00:17:36.370 --> 00:17:37.070
Pon.

00:17:38.160 --> 00:17:41.280
<i>So it's a pon this time, not a kan?</i>

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:44.040
<i>What are you trying to pull, Kiyosumi?</i>

00:17:48.100 --> 00:17:49.080
Kan.

00:18:01.550 --> 00:18:04.400
<i>I guess it's not guaranteed that she will win</i>

00:18:04.400 --> 00:18:06.370
<i>with the dead wall draw.</i>

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:08.940
Kan!

00:18:10.190 --> 00:18:11.520
<i>An open kan?!</i>

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:18.110
<i>It's not a rinshan kaihou.</i>

00:18:21.780 --> 00:18:22.410
Tsumo.

00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:24.630
2,000. 3,900.

00:18:25.970 --> 00:18:27.660
Another win for Kiyosumi!

00:18:28.110 --> 00:18:32.420
With this win, Kiyosumi is now in the lead!

00:18:32.770 --> 00:18:35.330
Which means all four schools have been

00:18:35.330 --> 00:18:38.420
in the lead during the second half of this match.

00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:40.720
The turnover rate is intense.

00:18:41.700 --> 00:18:46.310
At the end of South Hand 1, 
Eisui Girls' is in second place,

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:48.430
Miyamori Girls' is in third,

00:18:48.430 --> 00:18:51.240
and Himematsu High School is in last.

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:54.690
However, only 18,000 points 
separate last from first.

00:18:55.120 --> 00:18:59.320
Anything can still happen 
in the next three hands.

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:04.950
<i>She won again, and not 
even with a rinshan kaihou.</i>

00:19:05.570 --> 00:19:08.330
<i>She called the kan to pull 
in the tile she needed.</i>

00:19:08.820 --> 00:19:12.210
<i>She used the other player's 
discards to get additional draws.</i>

00:19:12.640 --> 00:19:16.280
<i>She's super amazing!</i>

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:22.390
South Hand 2

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:22.390
Dealer - Suehara Kyouko

00:19:35.940 --> 00:19:36.400
Kan!

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:39.280
<i>Again?!</i>

00:19:50.310 --> 00:19:50.750
Tsumo.

00:19:51.180 --> 00:19:52.620
2,000. 4,000.

00:19:53.400 --> 00:19:55.630
And yet another rinshan kaihou!

00:19:55.630 --> 00:19:58.380
<i>This time, it was a regular rinshan kaihou!</i>

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:00.880
<i>She's getting everything her way!</i>

00:20:03.430 --> 00:20:05.600
South Hand 3

00:20:06.930 --> 00:20:09.830
East Player
Kiyosumi High School (Nagano)
 Fifth Player - 1st Year
 Miyanaga Saki

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:18.090
South Player
